Runs for switching the exchange core to the codec (branch integrate), 2026-10-28, on the build host:
Lean v4.34.1 in localhost/b8perf-lean, AFL++ 5.04a in its pinned image, all through
LEAN_HTTP_REMOTE_DIR=lean-http-integrate.  The host was shared and loaded throughout (load average
about 100-280 on 128 CPUs).  Code commits: the final tree is integrate ed36708; the runs marked 25fb963
ran on the commit of that name before the history was tidied (branch integrate-log).  Its code
differs from ed36708's only in LeanHttp/Exchange/Response.lean (the second review's fixes to two
theorem statements and their docstrings, and shorter proof lines), which nothing but the proofs
imports; suites/final-ed36708 has the build (no warnings) and the axioms after that change.

suites/          run-suites.sh (here), copied to the box as out/run-suites.sh:
  final-ed36708/   $ LEAN_HTTP_REMOTE_DIR=lean-http-integrate scripts/remote.sh bash -c 'lake build; lake env lean scripts/proof-axioms.lean'
                   (incremental, with Response's build products removed first): build.txt, proof-axioms.txt.
  final-25fb963/   from a remote dir with .lake/build removed first:
                   $ ssh buildhost 'cd ~/lean-http-integrate && rm -rf .lake/build out/final'
                   $ LEAN_HTTP_REMOTE_DIR=lean-http-integrate scripts/remote.sh bash out/run-suites.sh out/final
                   build (no warnings), build-tests, proof-axioms (41 exchange theorems) and codec-axioms
                   (41 codec theorems), each on propext, Classical.choice and Quot.sound at most; unit,
                   codec (request encodings and the 41 response shapes through the core), response-codec,
                   traces, props-seed{1,2} (props 200000), explore-10, diff-seed{1..4} (codec-diff <seed>
                   60000 60000), diff-control, compare-seed{1,2} (core-tests compare 200000 <seed>).  All
                   exit 0.
  main-dbfc460/    the same script on main (git archive dbfc460, with this worktree's vendor/, unpacked
                   into out/main on the box and run there with podman directly, as remote.sh does):
                   the baseline.  codec.txt's 41 shape lines and codec-diff's classes and counts are the
                   same as the branch's (diff-seed*: "core" there is "machine" here).
  branch-c61733b/  the same script at c61733b (before the release change and the codec-diff reuse fix):
                   its codec-diff shows the "CORE vs codec ... reuse" classes that the fix explains.

bench/           codec-bench and the cross-binary comparison, each cell pinned to CPU 101:
  bench-100.txt    $ taskset --cpu-list 101 .lake/build/bin/codec-bench 100 1   (at 25fb963's code)
  xbench-40.txt    $ bash out/bench/xbench.sh 40   (xbench.sh here: main's codec-bench, from out/main, and
                   the branch's in turn, one block each, order drawn per block)
  ratios.txt       $ ./xratio.py bench-100.txt xbench-40.txt   (uv script here: paired ratios per block,
                   median with a distribution-free 95% interval)

net/             $ LEAN_HTTP_REMOTE_DIR=lean-http-integrate CTR_EXTRA='--sysctl net.ipv4.tcp_syn_retries=2' scripts/remote.sh bash tests/net/run.sh
                 76 passed, 0 failed, 1 known limitation (dns-timeout's exit, crashing with 139 as NOTES.md
                 says), as on main (logs/2026-10-28/core/net/summary.txt).  run.log is the console.
                 strace-nodelay.txt: $ ssh buildhost 'cd ~/lean-http-integrate && bash tests/net/strace-nodelay.sh'

fuzz/            The harness at 25fb963's code (Fuzz/Harness.lean as in c0cb963).
  replay/, replay-summary.txt, allow-summary.txt
                   replay.sh and allow.sh (here) inside the Lean image: every input of the copied corpora
                   (out/corpus on the box: ~/lean-http-fuzz2/out/{seeds,cmin,old-inputs} and the queues of
